{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975048-how-to-name-a-spirit","id":975048,"title":"How to Name a Spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-23T07:50:28-07:00","id":975048,"title":"How to Name a Spirit","content":"Hey, I've been reading through Axis Mundi for my Mage game, and saw the bit that said that all spirits have a True name, and knowing this name allows you a level of dominion over said spirit.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone here had any advice for creating unique names for various spirits.<br /> <br /> Is there a certain type of formula that you use?<br /> Do you just pluck names out of ancient languages?<br /> Are there naming conventions based on broods?<br /> Do you just keep it simple and give them &quot;this is the thing I do&quot; type names &quot;e.g. Leaf Walker&quot;<br /> Do you go complex and delve into history within the lore? If so what do you draw from for various broods?<br /> <br /> If there are any books out there which give advice on this sort of thing, let me know. My knowledge of Werewolf lore is limited to pretty much just Umbra and some Spirit stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, to all Gaffs get True Names, or is it something that's reserved for Jags and higher?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:40:24-07:00","id":975479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975048-how-to-name-a-spirit#post975048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I've been reading through Axis Mundi for my Mage game, and saw the bit that said that all spirits have a True name, and knowing this name allows you a level of dominion over said spirit.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if anyone here had any advice for creating unique names for various spirits.<br /> <br /> Is there a certain type of formula that you use?<br /> Do you just pluck names out of ancient languages??</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft (Chtulu Myth's creator) had an interesting system.<br /> For his &quot;dead unholy languages&quot; he juxtaposed particles from old dead (or at least near-extinct) languages. If I remember correctly, one of those was a variant of the Algonquian language.<br /> I don't know if he used random juxtaposition or set grammatical rules (being Lovecraft, probably the latter), but maybe is worth a shot.<br /> You can try the same with some old language from your area, after all with wikipedia and similar is simple to get some 20 words and a scarn grammatical rules (on the level &quot;-mn turn in -nn at the end of words&quot; ). Then you randomly associate parts of the words and tie them with those grammatical rules.<br /> I did something along these lines for <i>something</i> I'm writing, using some ancient italic language, and it didn't took more than 20 minutes to get an effective name-generation system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 09-24-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 201